        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "9e3aa537-cb51-3cbf-9596-8b7aa43a3473",
                "word": "diglossie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "866b0d57-5d34-4367-824f-1009c8f6461d",
                        "entry_id": "9e3aa537-cb51-3cbf-9596-8b7aa43a3473",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "diglossies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "685d538c-29f9-3289-a936-eba3d25ea50d",
                        "entry_id": "9e3aa537-cb51-3cbf-9596-8b7aa43a3473",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Cohabitation de deux langues parmi une même population, l’une d’elles étant pressentie comme formelle et l’autre comme inférieure et impropre à certains usages formels."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9dbd17d4-2450-472d-8913-92585b2b7bc6",
                                "sense_id": "685d538c-29f9-3289-a936-eba3d25ea50d",
                                "text": "Car l’ordonnance de Villers-Cotterêts visait d’abord le latin judiciaire, cette langue d’initiés qui protégeait l’emprise des juristes sur la fonction royale. Briser la diglossie propre au gouvernement médiéval n’allait pas sans rencontrer de résistance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3cc2e6fd-cabb-4e18-8313-f0456f5c13c6",
                                "sense_id": "685d538c-29f9-3289-a936-eba3d25ea50d",
                                "text": "Une telle situation rend la survie du sarde plus difficile que jamais et condamne les sardophones a un statut de diglossie, loin du bilinguisme souhaité, dans lequel leur langue apparait cantonnée, plus que jamais, à des situations de communication limitées."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ce7a18d-8c29-4634-a822-9b4012a112e7",
                                "sense_id": "685d538c-29f9-3289-a936-eba3d25ea50d",
                                "text": "Les études quantitatives sur le bilinguisme inuit […] montrent une nette pénétration de l’anglais aux dépens de l’inuktitut, dans tous les domaines de l’existence. C’est cette pénétration qui a entraîné la disparition presque totale des dialectes inuvialuit du delta et de la côte du Mackenzie, où le conflit linguistique lié à la diglossie a mené à la victoire, définitive semble-t-il, de la langue dominante."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3ad0d3e2-6bc9-465f-a89c-9958319b3ae7",
                        "source_entry_id": "9e3aa537-cb51-3cbf-9596-8b7aa43a3473",
                        "source_sense_id": "685d538c-29f9-3289-a936-eba3d25ea50d",
                        "target_lang_word": "Diglossie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Diglossie",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0374b1d5-6f36-3baa-b700-8d0fad4d94f2",
                                        "entry_id": "fd69284b-d58d-3fdf-8dfc-9def4241702d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Vorkommen von zwei Varietäten einer Sprache oder zwei Sprachen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "268fa7f5-e35d-488e-97fc-406a8f1046c9",
                                                "sense_id": "0374b1d5-6f36-3baa-b700-8d0fad4d94f2",
                                                "text": "„Die deutschsprachige Schweiz ist ein Gebiet medialer Diglossie.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "534378a0-c9c5-402a-b2b0-a2f081eb4b7e",
                                                "sense_id": "0374b1d5-6f36-3baa-b700-8d0fad4d94f2",
                                                "text": "Meist wird betont, dass Diglossie darin bestehe, dass zwei Varietäten einer Sprache, die ein unterschiedliches Prestige haben, je nach Situation verwenden werden; aber auch die Verwendung von zwei verschiedenen Sprachen kann mit Diglossie bezeichnet werden."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c0d42c2-6e95-4743-af6b-84b84f3352a2",
                                                "sense_id": "0374b1d5-6f36-3baa-b700-8d0fad4d94f2",
                                                "text": "„In einer durch Diglossie geprägten Umgebung kann die Wahl der einen oder anderen Varietät schnell zu einem Kennzeichen der sozialen Solidarität werden.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f68a760d-e623-4a81-a64b-0a886fa7d1cc",
                                                "sense_id": "0374b1d5-6f36-3baa-b700-8d0fad4d94f2",
                                                "text": "„An die Stelle der hebräisch-jiddischen Diglossie sollte eine voll entwickelte hochsprachliche Zweisprachigkeit von Hebräisch und der jeweiligen Landessprache der Juden treten.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "27401527-c5f9-4983-8b4d-8115017c26ff",
                        "source_entry_id": "9e3aa537-cb51-3cbf-9596-8b7aa43a3473",
                        "source_sense_id": "685d538c-29f9-3289-a936-eba3d25ea50d",
                        "target_lang_word": "diglossia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "diglossia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96de0cd1-ace7-3f9d-a581-d0cb5f1990ef",
                                        "entry_id": "f9da7a88-1e7e-349d-b11b-ba7cb8381a87",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The coexistence in a given population of two closely related native languages or dialects, one of which is regarded as more prestigious than the other; the similar coexistence of two unrelated languages."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28183d10-a36e-4ce4-a371-cf91eb3e241d",
                                                "sense_id": "96de0cd1-ace7-3f9d-a581-d0cb5f1990ef",
                                                "text": "To begin with, of the two varieties involved in diglossia, the one serving (H)igh societal functions, unlike that reserved for (L)ow ones, is nobody's mother tongue: it is learned in later life largely by formal education, and is not used for ordinary conversation. Secondly, the diglossic contrast concerns widely divergent varieties, as opposed to stylistic contrasts which tend to be small-scale. Moreover, diglossia occurs within a single language, while bilingualism or multilingualism, involve far more divergent linguistic systems."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb182e03-e5b7-4bd0-af43-e07d57b5c252",
                                                "sense_id": "96de0cd1-ace7-3f9d-a581-d0cb5f1990ef",
                                                "text": "2000, Joshua A. Fishman, Chapter 3: Bilingualism with and without diglossia; diglossia with and without bilingualism, Li Wei (editor), The Bilingualism Reader, Taylor & Francis (Routledge), page 81,\nIt is the purpose of this chapter to relate these two research traditions to each other by tracing the interaction between their two major constructs: bilingualism (on the part of psychologists) and diglossia (on the part of sociologists)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67d3cae8-1f30-4d42-a865-adb76fb615fd",
                                                "sense_id": "96de0cd1-ace7-3f9d-a581-d0cb5f1990ef",
                                                "text": "Only very small and isolated communities display neither diglossia nor bilingualism."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e5ab9297-ea46-3022-a965-27cc163e4459",
                                        "entry_id": "f9da7a88-1e7e-349d-b11b-ba7cb8381a87",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The presence of a cleft or doubled tongue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
